  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kanind&#xe9;, a long-standing and trusted Indigenous rights organization in Rond&#xf4;nia and southern Amazonas, works with projects strengthening Indigenous autonomy through territorial protection, food security, sustainable livelihoods, and institutional capacity. The project targets five territories covering 3.3 million hectares and about 1,500 people. Expected results include stronger organizations, enhanced women&#x2019;s leadership, trained environmental agents, and improved forest protection.</narrative>
